---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'Payment Guide — How to Use Alipay & WeChat Pay';
const description = 'Step-by-step guide for foreigners to set up Alipay and WeChat Pay in China.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="en">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <header class="py-12 text-center">
      <div class="text-sm text-brand-600 font-medium mb-2">CATEGORY</div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900  ">Payment Guide</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-500  ">How to use Alipay & WeChat Pay as a foreigner in China.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-gray  ">
      <div class="bg-amber-50  :border-amber-900 rounded-xl p-4 mb-8">
        <p class="text-amber-800  ">
          <strong>Note:</strong> This page is a placeholder. Detailed step-by-step content will be added soon.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Why This Matters</h2>
      <p>China is largely a cashless society. To survive daily life — buying groceries, paying for taxis, ordering food — you need either Alipay or WeChat Pay.</p>

      <h2>Alipay Tour Pass</h2>
      <p>The easiest way for tourists: Alipay's "Tour Pass" lets you add a foreign credit card and spend up to ¥2,000 without a Chinese bank account.</p>

      <h2>WeChat Pay</h2>
      <p>Slightly harder to set up as a foreigner, but essential because most small vendors and individuals prefer WeChat Pay over Alipay.</p>

      <h2>Coming Soon</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Step-by-step screenshots for Alipay setup</li>
        <li>WeChat Pay setup with foreign credit card</li>
        <li>Troubleshooting common issues</li>
        <li>Alternative payment methods (cash, international cards)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
